From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build/config: survive a newer clang than upstream tests with

riscv64 builds this tree with oe-core's native clang rather than the
clang bundled in the SDK's buildtools, because CLANG_PATH:riscv64 points
at the native toolchain. That toolchain runs ahead of the one upstream
tests against, so each clang release turns another diagnostic on in
vendored third-party sources. Two changes, for two different mechanisms.

-Werror is dropped. Disabling diagnostics one at a time only defers the
next failure:

  double-conversion/src/bignum.cc:49:12: error: unused function template
    'BitSize' [-Werror,-Wunused-template]

  abseil-cpp/absl/synchronization/mutex.h:602:68: error:
    'lifetime_capture_by(this)' is deprecated [-Werror,-Wdeprecated-attributes]

harfbuzz needs more than that. It promotes whole groups to errors from
inside hb.hh:

  #pragma GCC diagnostic error "-Wunused"

and in clang -Wunused covers -Wunused-template. No command-line flag
overrides it, because the pragma re-enables the group as it is parsed, so
dropping -Werror leaves this failing:

  third_party/harfbuzz/src/hb-meta.hh:131:3: error: unused function
    template 'operator()' [-Werror,-Wunused-template]

HB_NO_PRAGMA_GCC_DIAGNOSTIC_ERROR is harfbuzz's own guard for that: it
skips the block promoting to error and leaves its other pragmas alone.
meta-flutter's rive-text recipe carries the same define for the same
reason.

Warnings still print in both cases.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific toolchain combination]
Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
---
diff --git a/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn b/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
--- a/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -69,7 +69,14 @@ config("compiler") {
   cflags_objcc = []
   swiftflags = []
   ldflags = []
-  defines = []
+
+  # harfbuzz promotes warning groups to errors from inside hb.hh
+  # (#pragma GCC diagnostic error "-Wunused"), which no command-line flag can
+  # override -- the pragma re-enables the group as it is parsed. clang 23
+  # reports unused function templates in hb-meta.hh, so the build fails there
+  # whatever -Werror does. This is harfbuzz's own escape hatch: it skips the
+  # block that promotes to error and leaves its other pragmas alone.
+  defines = [ "HB_NO_PRAGMA_GCC_DIAGNOSTIC_ERROR" ]
   configs = []
 
   # Platform-specific configs.
@@ -740,7 +747,13 @@ if (is_win) {
     "-Wno-unused-parameter",  # Unused function parameters.
   ]
 
-  if (!is_qnx) {
+  # -Werror removed: meta-flutter builds this tree for riscv64 with oe-core's
+  # native clang rather than the clang bundled in the SDK's buildtools, and
+  # that toolchain is far newer than the one upstream tests against. Each
+  # release turns another diagnostic on in vendored third-party sources --
+  # -Wunused-template in double-conversion, -Wdeprecated-attributes in
+  # abseil -- none of which is code this layer can fix. Warnings still print.
+  if (false) {
     default_warning_flags += [
       "-Werror",  # Warnings as errors.
     ]
